WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:02.869
-Welcome back, everybody.
We're here with LL Cool J.

00:00:02.869 --> 00:00:04.537
One of the things I read about
this festival that is so cool

00:00:04.537 --> 00:00:06.105
to me is not just that these
people are going to be

00:00:06.105 --> 00:00:08.208
performing
but also how many of them

00:00:08.208 --> 00:00:11.144
are bringing a culinary element.

00:00:11.144 --> 00:00:13.146
-So it's actually a festival.

00:00:13.146 --> 00:00:14.948
It's not just a concert.
It's an immersive day.

00:00:14.948 --> 00:00:17.250
It's an experience.
Big boom boxes. Break dance.

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:19.786
All kinds of crazy stuff.
We'll play "Salute the Sample,"

00:00:19.786 --> 00:00:22.221
which is a game where you guess
where the song sample came from.

00:00:22.221 --> 00:00:25.558
-That's great.
-But there's also a food court.

00:00:25.558 --> 00:00:28.761
Bun B, curator.
He came up to me with the idea

00:00:28.761 --> 00:00:30.997
of curating this
Trill Meal food court.

00:00:30.997 --> 00:00:34.367
Him and a friend.
And what happens is

00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:37.303
you'll have like Nas' Sweet
Chick restaurant out there.

00:00:37.303 --> 00:00:40.507
E-40 will have Goon with
the Spoon out there.

00:00:40.507 --> 00:00:42.609
You'll have Mia X Whip Dem Pots.

00:00:42.609 --> 00:00:45.912
Jadakiss and Styles P
have Juice for Life.

00:00:45.912 --> 00:00:49.449
You have Ghostface Killah's
Killah Koffee out there.

00:00:49.449 --> 00:00:51.284
So it's like, when you come,

00:00:51.284 --> 00:00:53.219
you're going to be immersed
into hip-hop.

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:56.756
So, even if you -- like, if you
never really understood hip-hop

00:00:56.756 --> 00:00:58.857
or if it was a world that you
didn't really --

00:00:58.857 --> 00:01:01.527
you know, you just want to kind
of be a fly on the wall,

00:01:01.527 --> 00:01:04.897
this is like that moment to be
like holy [bleep]

00:01:04.897 --> 00:01:06.833
[ Laughter ]
"Yo, this is it.

00:01:06.833 --> 00:01:08.234
This is the one."
You know what I mean?

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:09.602
This is
the Rock the Bells festival.

00:01:09.602 --> 00:01:10.636
It's the real deal.
-That's really great.

00:01:10.636 --> 00:01:12.972
So, you were 16 years old
when you signed.

00:01:12.972 --> 00:01:14.507
-Yes.

00:01:14.507 --> 00:01:15.841
-Was your first song,
"I Need a Beat"?

00:01:15.841 --> 00:01:17.210
-Yes.
-Okay.

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:18.211
Do you remember the first rap --

00:01:18.211 --> 00:01:19.412
Was that the first one
you wrote?

00:01:19.412 --> 00:01:20.746
-Oh, no.
-Okay.

00:01:20.746 --> 00:01:23.549
-I've been rhym-- I started --
I became a fan of rap

00:01:23.549 --> 00:01:27.153
around 9 years old, of hip-hop,
of emceeing,

00:01:27.153 --> 00:01:29.289
and around 11 or 12,
I started writing.

00:01:29.289 --> 00:01:31.324
-Do you remember any of
your early lyrics?

00:01:31.324 --> 00:01:33.659
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.659 --> 00:01:36.096
-I mean, I got stuff so silly,
like -- I mean,

00:01:36.096 --> 00:01:38.431
the very first ever rhyme
I wrote, like,

00:01:38.431 --> 00:01:40.132
I must've been like
11 years old.

00:01:40.132 --> 00:01:42.769
[ Rapping ]
When you get off the wall
and you bust your balls.

00:01:42.769 --> 00:01:45.271
[ Skatting ]

00:01:45.271 --> 00:01:47.907
I'm gonna rock you up,
I gonna rock you down.

00:01:47.907 --> 00:01:50.043
And I'mma do it just for you.

00:01:50.043 --> 00:01:51.310
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.310 --> 00:01:53.746
♪ For those of you
who don't know me ♪

00:01:53.746 --> 00:01:57.917
♪ I be the famous rappin'
Rapper T ♪

00:01:57.917 --> 00:01:59.151
Stuff like that,
you know what I mean?

00:01:59.151 --> 00:02:00.719
-There you go.
I think it holds up petty well.

00:02:00.719 --> 00:02:01.754
[ Cheers and applause ]
Holds up pretty well.

00:02:01.754 --> 00:02:03.556
-It changed a lot.

00:02:03.556 --> 00:02:06.625
-Giant decision, obviously,
in a young rap career

00:02:06.625 --> 00:02:08.627
is when you pick your rap name.
-Without a doubt.

00:02:08.627 --> 00:02:12.098
-LL Cool J, can't imagine you
as anything else now.

00:02:12.098 --> 00:02:14.600
Did you have a second option?
-Absolutely.

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:18.371
-Do you have one that
you're so happy you dodged?

00:02:18.371 --> 00:02:21.641
-Uh... [ Laughs ]
Yeah, yeah.

00:02:21.641 --> 00:02:24.544
'Cause Deluxe kind of sounds
like a Happy Meal of some sort.

00:02:24.544 --> 00:02:26.679
[ Laughter ]
Some sort of -- I don't know.

00:02:26.679 --> 00:02:29.415
It's like some sort of
food-assist thing

00:02:29.415 --> 00:02:31.583
or a vacuum cleaner.
I don't know.

00:02:31.583 --> 00:02:33.419
So Deluxe wasn't going to work.

00:02:33.419 --> 00:02:34.987
Jay Ski.

00:02:34.987 --> 00:02:37.623
I didn't really understand the
connotations of that back then.

00:02:37.623 --> 00:02:39.158
The snow.
-Oh, right, right, right.

00:02:39.158 --> 00:02:41.194
-Jay Ski,
so that didn't really work.

00:02:41.194 --> 00:02:43.729
Because that wouldn't have
scaled well.

00:02:43.729 --> 00:02:46.832
And then --
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.832 --> 00:02:49.301
You know, the other names
was just moments in time.

00:02:49.301 --> 00:02:50.969
But, you know,
I remember going through

00:02:50.969 --> 00:02:52.271
the Jay Ski Cool J thing.

00:02:52.271 --> 00:02:54.440
I had a big moment being
a little 8-year--

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:56.242
well, maybe about 10 years old.

00:02:56.242 --> 00:02:58.878
11? Well, maybe about 12
at that time.

00:02:58.878 --> 00:03:02.515
-So, at 12 you decided
LL Cool J.

00:03:02.515 --> 00:03:04.650
-No, I decided on Cool J.
-Oh, Cool J.

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:07.987
-Cool J. And then I was hanging
with my man Mikey D.

00:03:07.987 --> 00:03:09.822
We used to run around
in Laurelton, Queens.

00:03:09.822 --> 00:03:13.059
And, you know, his name was
Playboy Mikey D.

00:03:13.059 --> 00:03:14.460
And then he had another friend

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:17.096
that was Red Hot Lovers
and this and that.

00:03:17.096 --> 00:03:18.731
So I was like -- Mike was like,

00:03:18.731 --> 00:03:20.666
"Yo, but you got to have
something with the girls."

00:03:20.666 --> 00:03:21.967
So, I'm like, "Yeah."

00:03:21.967 --> 00:03:23.670
He's like, "How about something
like Ladies Love?"

00:03:23.670 --> 00:03:25.304
And I'm like,
"Yeah, that's what it is.

00:03:25.304 --> 00:03:27.006
Ladies Love Cool J."

00:03:27.006 --> 00:03:29.041
So I just -- you know,
it's like wishful thinking.

00:03:29.041 --> 00:03:34.347
You know how you are. You know,
15, 16, Ladies Love cool J.

00:03:34.347 --> 00:03:36.382
It just felt so right, you know?

00:03:36.382 --> 00:03:39.919
-Now, when you told ladies
in those early years

00:03:39.919 --> 00:03:42.989
what the LL stood for,
did they think

00:03:42.989 --> 00:03:45.591
it was a fair name
to give yourself?

00:03:45.591 --> 00:03:46.592
Ladies Love Cool J?

00:03:46.592 --> 00:03:47.827
[ Laughter ]

00:03:47.827 --> 00:03:49.295
Were they like,
"What's the LL for?"

00:03:49.295 --> 00:03:51.097
-That's a hit and miss, bro.

00:03:51.097 --> 00:03:53.766
You know, that doesn't have to
go over well.

00:03:53.766 --> 00:03:55.468
It can, you know what I mean?

00:03:55.468 --> 00:03:57.069
But it doesn't have to, right?
-Yeah.

00:03:57.069 --> 00:03:59.038
-That's kind of like a --
You know what I mean?

00:03:59.038 --> 00:04:01.907
It's not a panacea.
Let's put it like that.

00:04:01.907 --> 00:04:04.344
You know what I mean? You're not
going to cure it all with that.

00:04:04.344 --> 00:04:07.980
-No. You've been married
for a very long time.

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:09.949
You have four wonderful
children.

00:04:09.949 --> 00:04:11.183
-Yeah.

00:04:11.183 --> 00:04:13.285
-How did you first
meet your wife?

00:04:13.285 --> 00:04:15.988
-I met her on Easter Day
in Queens.

00:04:15.988 --> 00:04:18.558
Just, you know, I was walking
around the block

00:04:18.558 --> 00:04:21.427
and she was with her cousin
or something.

00:04:21.427 --> 00:04:23.396
I was like, "Yo, you know,
you should come around."

00:04:23.396 --> 00:04:24.664
She said, "You come around."

00:04:24.664 --> 00:04:26.766
"Eh. Give me your number,"
you know what I'm saying?

00:04:26.766 --> 00:04:28.801
She gave me her number
and you know.

00:04:28.801 --> 00:04:30.436
-How many years now?
-It's all cool.

00:04:30.436 --> 00:04:31.770
I called up. She said, "Hello."

00:04:31.770 --> 00:04:33.239
I said, "You know, you sound
like a truck driver."

00:04:33.239 --> 00:04:35.241
[ Laughter ]
You know what I mean?

00:04:35.241 --> 00:04:37.110
And then we just went
from there.

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:38.878
[ Laughter ]

00:04:38.878 --> 00:04:41.313
-That's how they all start.
-Oh, yeah.

00:04:41.313 --> 00:04:43.649
-One of the better
pickup lines is,

00:04:43.649 --> 00:04:44.817
"You sound like a truck driver."

00:04:44.817 --> 00:04:46.085
[ Laughter ]

00:04:46.085 --> 00:04:47.386
-It probably is.
-It worked, it worked.

00:04:47.386 --> 00:04:49.488
-It actually is pretty good.
It actually is.

00:04:49.488 --> 00:04:51.457
-This is thrilling as well with
everything else going on.

00:04:51.457 --> 00:04:53.292
You're working on new music.

00:04:53.292 --> 00:04:55.027
-Yes, yes,
I'm working on new music.

00:04:55.027 --> 00:04:56.628
I actually just finished
my new album.

00:04:56.628 --> 00:04:58.531
-Oh, that's exciting.
-Yeah, I finished a new album.

00:04:58.531 --> 00:04:59.999
[ Cheer and applause ]
Thank you, thank you,

00:04:59.999 --> 00:05:02.735
thank you, yeah.

00:05:02.735 --> 00:05:04.770
It was executive produced by
Q-Tip.

00:05:04.770 --> 00:05:06.472
-Oh, that's great.
-He did the whole record.

00:05:06.472 --> 00:05:07.907
Q-Tip from A Tribe Called Quest.

00:05:07.907 --> 00:05:10.442
He produced the whole record
from front to back.

00:05:10.442 --> 00:05:13.679
And, you know, the question,
a lot of times especially

00:05:13.679 --> 00:05:15.715
with a guy that's been out
as long as I have,

00:05:15.715 --> 00:05:18.284
Hall of Fame, Grammys
and all that, 1,000 years,

00:05:18.284 --> 00:05:21.187
most people say, it's like, "Oh,
you got a new album coming out?

00:05:21.187 --> 00:05:23.322
Isn't that sweet?
Let me hear the hits."

00:05:23.322 --> 00:05:24.957
You know, it's kind of like,

00:05:24.957 --> 00:05:27.426
"Poor baby, he's working on
a new album."

00:05:27.426 --> 00:05:29.395
[ Laughter ]
Right?

00:05:29.395 --> 00:05:30.663
But I'm you telling you, like,

00:05:30.663 --> 00:05:33.099
we put something together that I
think is pretty special.

00:05:33.099 --> 00:05:35.167
I hope you like it
when you hear it.

00:05:35.167 --> 00:05:37.303
Most people always say, "Okay,

00:05:37.303 --> 00:05:38.604
so you're working on
a new album.

00:05:38.604 --> 00:05:40.506
So either you're going to be
stuck in a time warp,

00:05:40.506 --> 00:05:43.176
taking it back,
or you're going to be trying to

00:05:43.176 --> 00:05:45.111
pretend you're 19
and look ridiculous."

00:05:45.111 --> 00:05:48.080
Which one is it going to be?
And it's actually neither one.

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:51.984
Actually, you know, Q-Tip helped
me break some new ground.

00:05:51.984 --> 00:05:54.386
And I think some of the topics
and the messaging

00:05:54.386 --> 00:05:57.056
that I'm talking about I think
are relevant to the world.

00:05:57.056 --> 00:05:59.459
And I think that it's proof that

00:05:59.459 --> 00:06:01.193
hip-hop culture
can grow and expand.

00:06:01.193 --> 00:06:03.862
And I just want to show people
what's possible musically.

00:06:03.862 --> 00:06:06.499
And to be honest, that person
that that inspired me

00:06:06.499 --> 00:06:10.369
in a lot of ways was Santana
in the fact that he came after

00:06:10.369 --> 00:06:12.939
so long and did some
really interesting music

00:06:12.939 --> 00:06:15.641
many, many, years later, and I
found that to be inspiring.

00:06:15.641 --> 00:06:18.377
-Well, I can't wait.
I think we're all very excited.

00:06:18.377 --> 00:06:19.711
Hey, thanks so much
for being here. What a delight.

00:06:19.711 --> 00:06:21.380
-My man. Great to be here.

00:06:21.380 --> 00:06:23.883
-LL Cool J, Rock the Bells.
-Rock the Bells, baby.

00:06:23.883 --> 00:06:25.951
-Takes place Saturday,
Forest Hills Stadium.

00:06:25.951 --> 00:06:28.054
For tickets go to
rockthebells.com.

00:06:28.054 --> 00:06:30.056
We'll be right back
with Cristin Milioti.

